{"toolCallId":"call_ef8fa2ee822f455fb02302eb3e3bbdb4","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"133:    \"rule_id\": \"SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY\",\n134-    \"aliases\": [\n135-      \"SUFFICIENCY\",\n136-      \"DOC_SUFFICIENCY\"\n137-    ],\n138-    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n139-    \"severity\": \"error\",\n140-    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n141-    \"description\": \"Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\"\n142-  },\n143-  {\n144-    \"rule_id\": \"CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION\",\n145-    \"aliases\": [\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"16c288","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_efc5600268de4306914e74e1aa1102eb","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n1. **Upgrade level:** If content is complex, change `| **Level** | 1 |` to `| **Level** | 2 |`\n2. **Reduce scope:** Split complex specs into multiple smaller specs\n3. **Add content:** For sparse specs, add missing user stories, phases, or tasks\n\n---\n\n## 10. AI_PROTOCOLS\n\n**Severity:** ERROR\n**Description:** Validates that Level 3 and 3+ specs include AI execution protocol sections for agent guidance. For Level 3+, missing protocol components are reported as errors.\n\n### Required for Level 3+\n\n| Component             | Location        | Purpose                           |\n| --------------------- | --------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| AI Execution section  | plan/tasks.md   | Main protocol header              |\n| Pre-Task Checklist    | plan/tasks.md   | Steps before starting any task    |\n| Execution Rules       | plan/tasks.md   | TASK-SEQ, TASK-SCOPE constraints  |\n| Status Format         | plan/tasks.md   | How to report progress            |\n| Blocked Protocol      | plan/tasks.md   | What to do when stuck             |\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Level 3: Should have protocol section (warning if missing)\n- Level 3+: Must have at least 3/4 components (error if fewer)\n- Phase parent: skipped. Under the lean trio policy its `plan.md` and `tasks.md` live in the child folders, which carry the protocol.\n\n### Detection Patterns\n\n```markdown\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL         ← Main section\n### Pre-Task Checklist           ← Component 1\n### Execution Rules              ← Component 2\n### Status Reporting Format      ← Component 3\n### Blocked Task Protocol        ← Component 4\n```\n\n### Examples\n\n**Pass (Level 3+):**\n```markdown\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n- [ ] Read relevant files\n- [ ] Verify preconditions\n\n### Execution Rules\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Complete tasks in order |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Only modify files in scope |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\nAfter each task: \"Task T## complete. Files modified: [list]\"\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\nIf blocked: Stop, document blocker, request help\n```\n\n### How to Fix\n\nAdd the AI Execution Protocol section to plan.md or tasks.md. Reference the Level 3 templates:\n\n```bash\n# See protocol examples in templates\ncat .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/plan.md.tmpl\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. LEVEL_MATCH\n\n**Severity:** ERROR\n**Description:** Validates that the declared level is consistent across all spec folder files and required files exist.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"631084","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_f22810c5164f401baaee8bd73ed15a45","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"SCORE_RISK=$(calculate_risk_score)\nSCORE_COMPLEXITY=$(calculate_complexity_score)\n\nTOTAL_SCORE=$((SCORE_LOC + SCORE_FILES + SCORE_RISK + SCORE_COMPLEXITY))\n\n# Determine recommended level\ndetermine_level \"$TOTAL_SCORE\"\n\n# Calculate confidence\ncalculate_confidence\n\n# Calculate phase recommendation (default on; opt-out via --no-recommend-phases)\nif [[ \"$RECOMMEND_PHASES\" = true ]]; then\n  determine_phasing\nfi\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 7. OUTPUT RESULTS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nif [[ \"$JSON_OUTPUT\" = true ]]; then\n  output_json\nelse\n  output_text\nfi\n\nexit 0\n\n# Exit codes:\n#   0 - Success\n#   1 - ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"451605","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_f6d0e68261a44065bb11158d6b267a64","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Phase 2: rebuild-fanout-removal\"\ndescription: \"Ordered tasks for the rebuild fan-out removal: the D1 decision and a pre-change capture, the token and its test in one commit, the spec-kit-check trigger, then three rebuild observations and the 24 h baseline.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"rebuild fanout removal tasks\"\n  - \"phase 2 rebuild fanout removal tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Phase 2: rebuild-fanout-removal\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`, followed by a `File:` line naming the path and line, a quoted anchor, a `Change:` line, a fenced `Check:` block with its `Expected:` result, a `Rollback:` line and a `Stop and escalate if:` line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n### T001 DECISION D1 (operator yes required) - choose how rebuild commits skip CI (AC-001)\n\nFile: `specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/002-rebuild-fanout-removal/scratch/d1-answer.md` (exists; written 2026-10-23 with the operator's answer). Anchor: the answer line.\n\nDefault: option A, the `[skip ci]` token on the commit body line at `.github/workflows/trigger-index-rebuild.yml:149`. It is one line, needs no filter entries and adds no new YAML pattern.\n\nAlternative: option B, a push-only `paths-ignore:` on the 9 unfiltered workflows plus `!` negations on the 4 path-filtered ones. That is 8 entries each, 104 in total across 13 files, plus an amendment to ordering rule 2, for about 2,002 runner-min/day with `message-contract` left unfiltered.\n\nChange: the operator answered on 2026-10-23, and the file already holds the answer. Do not re-ask and do not rewrite the file; this task only runs the existing check.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/002-rebuild-fanout-removal/scratch\ncat specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/002-rebuild-fanout-removal/scratch/d1-answer.md\n```\n\nExpected: `D1=A`.\n\nRollback: delete `scratch/d1-answer.md`.\n\nStop and escalate if: the operator answers B, or no answer arrives. This task list implements option A only; B replaces T004 to T007 and T010 to T011 with the ignore edit set and makes T008 and T009 assert the ignore instead of the token.\n\n---\n\n### T002 Capture the pre-change fan-out for three rebuild SHAs (AC-005)\n\nFile: `specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/002-rebuild-fanout-removal/scratch/pre-change/` (new directory). Anchor: none.\n\nChange: create one `gh run list` JSON per rebuild SHA, so AC-005 has a before number.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/002-rebuild-fanout-removal/scratch/pre-change\ngit log --format='%H %s' -40 origin/main | grep 'rebuild the trigger index' | head -3\n```\n\nExpected: three lines, each a full SHA followed by `chore(system-spec-kit): rebuild the trigger index`.\n\nThen, for each of the three SHAs, replace `<sha>` and run:\n\n```bash\ngh run list --commit <sha> --json databaseId,workflowName,event,conclusion --limit 30 \\\n  > specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/002-rebuild-fanout-removal/scratch/pre-change/<sha>.json\n```\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"6f68ba","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
